Popular Mac app AppZapper was today revamped with a new design, updated functionality, and a fresh name. <a href="https://appzapper.com/">AppZapper 3000</a> offers a quick way to delete Mac apps and their associated files.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/appzapper3000.jpg" alt="" width="1597" height="934" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065044" /><br/>
AppZapper requires Full Disk Access permission to find files on the Mac. Once installed, you can drag and drop an app into AppZapper and then click on the Zap All button to remove the app and related files with a fun laser gun animation and sound. AppZapper locates and deletes all of an app's files in just a few seconds, and users can choose from four different themes.<br/>
<br/>
AppZapper first launched in 2006, so the new version is debuting on its 20th anniversary. Developer Austin Sarner says the updated version of the app is tailored to macOS security requirements and is better at finding related app files.<br/>
<br/>
The app can be downloaded for free and tested before purchasing. A license is priced at &#36;18 for a single user and &#36;29 for a family pack that allows the app to be used on up to five Macs. macOS 15 or later is required.<br/>
